# Database & backend (Hope Aviation)

## Source of truth

- **Schema**: `supabase/migrations/*.sql` — apply migrations to the linked Supabase project (`supabase db push` or dashboard SQL).
- **RLS**: Enabled on all `public` tables. Authorization uses `public.has_role(auth.uid(), 'admin' | 'instructor' | 'student')` (SECURITY DEFINER). Never bypass RLS from the browser; use the **service role** only in trusted server-only code when required.
- **Types**: `types/database.ts` mirrors tables; prefer `supabase gen types typescript --linked` when the remote schema changes.

## Data model (short)

- **Auth**: `profiles.id` = `auth.users.id`. New user rows are created by `public.handle_new_user` on `auth.users` insert.
- **Roles**: `roles` + `roles_users` (many-to-many). Seed slugs: `admin`, `instructor`, `student`.
- **i18n**: `title`, `description`, `content` JSONB keys like `{ "es": "...", "en": "..." }`.
- **Enums**: `courses.status` ∈ `draft|published|archived`; `enrollments.status` ∈ `active|completed|cancelled`.
- **Course staff**: `course_instructors` links `courses` and `profiles` (instructors). `public.is_course_instructor(user_id, course_id)` (SECURITY DEFINER) backs RLS so assigned instructors can read that course’s enrollments and related `lesson_progress`.

## Backend rules

- Validate and type all inputs (Zod or similar) before writes.
- Use the **server** Supabase client (`lib/supabase/server.ts`) for session-scoped queries; reserve `service_role` for admin scripts or exceptional server routes.
- Do not leak Supabase errors or stack traces to the client; return safe messages.
- Add indexes when introducing new filter/sort paths; avoid N+1 (batch joins or nested selects).

## Changing the schema

1. Add a new timestamped file under `supabase/migrations/`.
2. Keep RLS policies updated when adding tables or columns.
3. Regenerate TypeScript types after deploy.
